@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Theory boundary
+
+Decision: no bend2/bend.ts theory edit is admitted by this ranked deepening.
+
+Deletion test
+Remove the proposed theory edit and ask whether any required capability disappears.
+
+1. Context routing lives in main.ts and guide/agent.
+2. PROGRAM and PROVE are documentation packs.
+3. Stable diagnostics and JSON are a CLI seam.
+4. Proof moves document existing language forms.
+5. Dependency graphing traverses the already exported lowered term representation.
+6. Law and diagnostic indexes are data.
+7. The PROOF to LAWS import guard already exists upstream.
+8. Eval sidecars are process residue.
+9. --why and --pack are CLI routing sugar.
+
+Result: no required capability depends on a theory change.
+
+Reopen only if a future required result cannot be expressed by existing checked terms, exported term structure, CLI policy, compiler metadata, tests, or documentation. A harder proof is not a reopen condition.
